            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Italian for the press release, then the Italian for the denial."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: l'edizione",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "l'edizione — \"the edition; the news bulletin\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "L'edizione della sera ha una foto in prima pagina. The evening edition has a photo on the front page."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Un'edizione straordinaria — a special edition. On TV, l'edizione delle venti is the eight o'clock news."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "edizione is a learned borrowing from Latin ēditiō \"a putting forth, a publishing\" (Lewis & Short), from ēdere \"to give out\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
